  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "When Heaven Overseeing Tower strikes the ten extreme immortal zombie lifeless formation at Yi Tian Mountain, three more Immortal Gu Houses rise to meet the attack. Heaven Overseeing Tower Lord names Golden Altar among seven Shadow Sect Immortal Gu Houses forced onto the field: Sacred Feather City, Unbreakable Iron Fortress, Blood River Chariot, Nightmare Castle, Green Wave Pavilion, Weaving Cocoon Manor, and Golden Altar.",
      "chapters": [
        1004
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "house_heaven_overseeing_tower",
        "loc_yi_tian_mountain",
        "sys_immortal_gu_house",
        "char_heaven_overseeing_tower_lord",
        "fac_shadow_sect",
        "house_sacred_feather_city",
        "house_unbreakable_iron_fortress",
        "house_blood_river_chariot",
        "house_nightmare_castle",
        "house_green_wave_pavilion",
        "house_weaving_cocoon_manor"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "After Heaven Overseeing Tower’s fate-backed white light fades, Green Wave Pavilion, Weaving Cocoon Manor, and Golden Altar, the three houses closest to the tower, have broken apart. Their debris falls as Gu worms that look uninjured yet hold no life. The three houses have sacrificed themselves to endure that attack so the ten extreme formation can continue.",
      "chapters": [
        1004
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_gu_worms"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Deviation (recorded): this page uses the Southern Border region field because the house is first named and destroyed at Yi Tian Mountain. Golden Altar is a mobile Immortal Gu House, not a five-region map seat.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "reg_southern_border"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "After Shadow Sect is beaten down and Fang Yuan takes leadership, the remaining resources include twelve Immortal Gu House construction plans. Golden Altar is named in that list with Nightmare Castle, Green Wave Pavilion, Weaving Cocoon Manor, Sacred Feather City, and others.",
      "chapters": [
        1380
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "shadow-sect-construction-plan",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "When Fang Yuan builds an incomplete Immortal Gu House for joint battle with his subordinates, he takes reference from Golden Altar among many other Immortal Gu Houses, while the skeleton of the design is based on Graceful Chaotic Duel Stage.",
      "chapters": [
        1628
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "design-reference",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "house_graceful_chaotic_duel_stage"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Inside Crazed Demon Cave, Lady White Rabbit fields seven rank eight Immortal Gu Houses that Fang Yuan had assembled for his subordinates. Those houses are modified on the basis of Golden Altar and other Immortal Gu Houses, treated as partial innovations rather than wholly new designs.",
      "chapters": [
        2178
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "modified-descendants",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_crazed_demon_cave",
        "char_lady_white_rabbit"
      ]
    }
